    "important_interpretation": [
        "The raw coherent transform is not the same as the normalized EXP05 correlation state. The desired correlation amplitudes reside in the data-register zero-Walsh sector.",
        "A coherent outer-QAA preparation unitary therefore requires either sector amplitude amplification or a joint outer oracle that explicitly includes the data-register zero condition.",
        "EXP12 models the nested approach: first amplify the zero-Walsh sector, then use the resulting unitary as the state-preparation family A.",
        "The QROM cost is scenario-dependent because no gate-level hardware-specific QROM synthesis has been fixed.",
        "QROM stores only the eleven classical bits actually needed by the canonical linear relation rather than full plaintext and ciphertext blocks."
    ],
    "limitations": [
        "TE values are logical Toffoli-equivalent resource proxies, not physical fault-tolerant runtimes.",
        "QROM, inverse S-box, and multi-controlled-reflection costs are analytical resource models rather than transpiled hardware circuits.",
        "The near-deterministic sector preparation still contains residual non-zero-Walsh amplitude whenever Pgood < 1.",
        "EXP13 should model the outer good predicate as (data register = 0) AND verifier(key), avoiding any assumption that residual non-zero-Walsh amplitude has the desired key distribution."
    ]
